<title>RUSSIA: Austrian Airlines adds Ukraine route.</title>
<headline>Austrian Airlines adds Ukraine route.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Airlines launched regular non-stop passenger flights between Vienna and the southern Ukrainian city of Dnepropetrovsk on Tuesday, a spokesman at the airline's Moscow office said.</p>
<p>He said the carrier operates an 80-seat Fokker-70 aircraft on the route on Tuesdays and Saturdays and plans to add an additional weekly flight at the end of October.</p>
<p>Austrian Airlines already flies to eight cities in the former Soviet Union -- Moscow, St Petersburg, Kiev, Minsk, Almaty, Odessa, Riga and Vilnius.</p>
<p>-- Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
